Daniel J Barkalow (DBarkalo@world.std.com) wrote:
: I was wondering what affects the chances of a monster generating a 
: corpse. It seems that some monsters generate corpses almost every time, 
: while others (notably golems) never or infrequently generate corpses. In 
: particular, I was wondering if anyone else has noticed that a certain 
: kind of monster on a certain level (not to give a spoiler if it's true) 
: VERY rarely generates a (mm, tasty!) corpse. Perhaps a code-reading is in 
: order...

These are possible spoilers...

Well, corpse creation depends on several things.  Undead on a level
with a graveyard will rarely generate a corpse.  Large, huge, and
gargantuan monsters usually will.  Some (ghosts, for instance) will
never leave corpses.  Also, whether you kill a monster or it is
killed by something else (a trap, or a bolt of fire, for instance)
has some effect.  On a graveyard level, a wraith will generate a
corpse more often if you don't kill it (let another monster do the
dirty work or something).  I can't quote other stats right off the
top of my head, because I forgot to bring my spoilers.  There is a
file on just this subject at ftp.krl.caltech.edu, in pub/nethack.
It is quite complete.

